 "story": {
  "kicker": "Marigny",
  "h2": "The John",
  "paragraphs": [
   "The John is on Burgundy in the Marigny, in a building with blue shutters and a sign over the door that says nothing but JOHN. The joke is fully committed to: there are two toilets mounted against a purple wall inside, surrounded by photographs, and nobody offers an explanation. Past that it is a long wooden bar, stools down one side, neon, and a room that carries on back further than it looks from the street.",
   "Doors at ten in the morning and last call at three, which makes it a day bar and a late bar at once. There is a beer pong table at the back and an arcade machine near the door. The house drink is the Hennessy Margarita, which one reviewer describes as very tasty and powerful, in that order. The thing to sort out before you walk in is that the place is cash only."
  ]
 },
